**Code Explanation:**

The code aggregates the metrics computed in previous steps across the 10 independent realizations to assess the statistical significance of the findings. First, it re-calculates the empirical 3D radial density profile and the mass-conditioned gNFW fits for each realization individually, as the previous step only computed the aggregated fit. It then constructs a feature matrix containing the mean fractional 2PCF residual in the 1-halo regime (r < 5 Mpc/h), the Spearman rank correlation coefficient (luminosity vs. local density), and the gNFW fit parameters (normalization A and scale radius x_s) for both mass bins. Using this feature matrix, the code computes and prints the sample covariance and correlation matrices to identify any linear dependencies between the clustering anomalies and the fitted structural parameters. Finally, it generates a comprehensive 6-panel summary figure consolidating: 1. The mean empirical radial density profile with +/- 1 standard deviation error bands compared to the theoretical exponential decay. 2. The Void Probability Function (VPF) comparison between the empirical data and the KDE-based synthetic model. 3. The luminosity-dependent marked correlation function for all galaxies and satellites only. 4. The mass-conditioned gNFW fits to the empirical satellite radial density profiles. 5. A heatmap of the correlation matrix of the aggregated metrics. 6. The fractional 2PCF residuals (Delta xi / xi) with error bars, highlighting the scale at which the synthetic model deviates from the empirical data. The summary figure is saved as a high-resolution PNG, and the covariance/correlation matrices are saved to disk for further analysis.

